# BUG-221 — module init must be TRANSITIVE.
#
# The entry point used to initialise its DIRECT dependencies only, so a module
# reached at depth 2 never had `_allocator`/`_io` set and segfaulted at
# 0xffffffffffffffff on its first file touch. `main -> leaf` worked; adding one
# module in between crashed. Nothing exotic is needed to trigger it — three
# files and one File.exists call.
#
# Under `--runtime-module` the runtime holds ONE `_allocator`/`_io` that every
# module shares at any depth, and the entry point drives `_initModuleVars` over
# the TRANSITIVE dep list, so depth stops mattering. Without the flag this file
# still reproduces the crash — it is the before/after pair, not a pure negative.
use bug221_transitive_init_mid exposing viaMid

def main()
    print(viaMid("no_such_file.txt"))
